        <article class="policy">
            <div class="notice"><strong>Plain-language summary:</strong> We use the information needed to create and protect your account, process payments and utility purchases, provide receipts and support, prevent fraud, and improve JolaxPay. We do not sell your personal information.</div>

            <section id="scope"><h2>1. Who we are and the scope of this policy</h2><p>JolaxPay (referred to as “JolaxPay”, “we”, “us” or “our”) provides a mobile wallet and payment platform for utility purchases, transfers, withdrawals, receipts, scheduled purchases, support and related services. This policy applies to the JolaxPay mobile application, customer website, support channels and services that link to this policy.</p><p>For personal information processed to provide JolaxPay services, JolaxPay acts as the data controller. Certain payment institutions, banks, utility vendors and other service providers may separately act as controllers for information they receive under their own privacy notices.</p></section>

            <section id="information"><h2>2. Information we collect</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Examples</th><th>Why it is needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
                <tr><td>Account and identity</td><td>Name, email address, phone number, profile photograph, account type and verification status.</td><td>Registration, account management, identity and contact verification.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Transaction and wallet</td><td>Wallet address, balances, ledger entries, funding, transfers, withdrawals, bill type, amount, recipient, meter or customer identifier, provider references and receipts.</td><td>To request, process, reconcile and support transactions and maintain required records.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Bank and payment details</td><td>Bank name and code, account number and verified account name; payment-provider references and authorization results.</td><td>Wallet funding, bank withdrawals, refunds and fraud prevention. Card credentials entered on a provider’s checkout are handled by that payment provider and are not stored by JolaxPay.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Saved service information</td><td>Saved meters, beneficiaries, meter groups, schedules and Power Circle contacts.</td><td>To provide requested convenience and repeat-payment features.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Device and security</td><td>Device name, operating system, app version, IP address, session records, push token, login activity and security or fraud signals.</td><td>Authentication, session management, notifications, troubleshooting and protection against misuse.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Communications</td><td>Support tickets, chat messages, feedback, notification preferences and records of messages sent.</td><td>Customer support, service notices and dispute resolution.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Usage and insights</td><td>Feature interactions, purchase history, typical top-up amounts and insight engagement.</td><td>To operate product analytics and provide rules-based summaries or suggestions. JolaxPay’s current suggestions are generated from transaction patterns rather than an external generative-AI service.</td></tr>
            </tbody></table></div><p>We generally receive this information directly from you, your device, other JolaxPay users who transact with you, and the payment, banking or utility providers involved in your request.</p></section>

            <section id="use"><h2>3. How we use information</h2><ul><li>Create, verify, secure and administer your account.</li><li>Provide wallet funding, wallet-to-wallet transfers, bank withdrawals and utility purchases.</li><li>Verify meters, customer identifiers and bank accounts with the relevant provider.</li><li>Generate receipts, transaction history, summaries, repeat suggestions and scheduled-payment reminders.</li><li>Send verification codes, transaction updates, security alerts, announcements and messages you have allowed.</li><li>Detect unusual activity, enforce transaction limits, prevent fraud and protect users and the platform.</li><li>Reconcile provider responses, investigate failed or disputed transactions and provide support.</li><li>Understand service performance, fix faults and improve product usability.</li><li>Comply with applicable legal, regulatory, accounting and law-enforcement obligations.</li></ul><p>We do not sell or rent your personal information, and we do not use it for unrelated advertising by third parties.</p></section>

            <section id="basis"><h2>4. Our lawful bases</h2><p>Depending on the activity, we process personal information because it is necessary to perform our contract with you, comply with a legal obligation, pursue a legitimate interest such as security and service improvement, protect vital interests, or because you have given consent. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it at any time, although this does not affect processing already carried out lawfully.</p></section>

            <section id="sharing"><h2>5. When we share information</h2><p>We disclose only the information reasonably needed for the relevant service. Recipients may include:</p><ul><li><strong>Payment and banking providers</strong> used for collections, virtual accounts, account verification, transfers, refunds and withdrawals, including the provider currently selected by JolaxPay.</li><li><strong>Utility and value-added-service providers</strong> used to verify and fulfil electricity, airtime, data, television and education purchases.</li><li><strong>Communications providers</strong> that deliver email, SMS verification, push notifications and service messages.</li><li><strong>Hosting, storage, monitoring and realtime-service providers</strong> that help operate and secure the platform.</li><li><strong>Professional advisers, auditors, regulators, courts or law-enforcement bodies</strong> where disclosure is required or permitted by law.</li><li><strong>A successor organisation</strong> in connection with a genuine merger, financing, restructuring or transfer of the business, subject to appropriate safeguards.</li></ul><p>We require service providers acting on our instructions to use information only for the contracted purpose and to protect it appropriately.</p></section>

            <section id="transfers"><h2>6. International data transfers</h2><p>Some technology or communications providers may process information outside Nigeria. Where personal information is transferred internationally, we use measures required by applicable law, such as adequacy decisions, approved contractual safeguards, consent where appropriate, or another lawful transfer mechanism.</p></section>

            <section id="retention"><h2>7. How long we keep information</h2><p>We retain personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy. Account information is normally kept while your account remains active. Transaction, ledger, reconciliation, fraud, tax and regulatory records may be retained longer where required for financial recordkeeping, dispute handling, fraud prevention or legal compliance. Support and technical records are retained according to their operational need.</p><p>When information is no longer required, we delete it, anonymise it or securely isolate it, subject to lawful backup-retention cycles.</p></section>

            <section id="security"><h2>8. How we protect information</h2><p>We apply administrative, technical and organisational safeguards designed for the nature of the information we process. These include access controls, password hashing, one-time verification codes, session controls, encrypted network transport, transaction idempotency, audit records, fraud rules, provider reconciliation and restricted staff permissions.</p><p>No internet or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure. You should keep your password and verification codes confidential, use a secure device, and tell us promptly if you suspect unauthorised access.</p></section>

            <section id="rights"><h2>9. Your privacy rights</h2><p>Subject to the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and other applicable law, you may have the right to:</p><ul><li>be informed about how your information is processed;</li><li>request access to, or a copy of, your personal information;</li><li>correct inaccurate or incomplete information;</li><li>request erasure, restriction or objection in qualifying circumstances;</li><li>withdraw consent where consent is the lawful basis;</li><li>request portability of eligible information;</li><li>request human review where a decision based solely on automated processing has a legal or similarly significant effect; and</li><li>complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</li></ul><p>To exercise a right, contact us using the details below. We may need to verify your identity before acting. Some requests may be limited where retaining or processing information is required by law, necessary to complete a transaction, or needed to protect another person’s rights.</p></section>

            <section id="children"><h2>10. Children’s privacy</h2><p>JolaxPay is not directed to children and should not be used by anyone who cannot lawfully enter the agreement required to hold an account. We do not knowingly create accounts for children without the consent or other lawful authority required by applicable law. If you believe a child has provided personal information improperly, contact us so we can investigate.</p></section>

            <section id="cookies"><h2>11. Website and device data</h2><p>Our public website may receive ordinary server information such as IP address, browser type, requested page and request time for security and reliable delivery. The mobile application stores authentication and preference information on your device and may use camera access when you choose to scan a QR code, photo-library or camera access when you choose a profile image, biometric capability when enabled, and notification permissions when granted. You can manage device permissions in your phone settings, although disabling a permission may prevent the related feature from working.</p></section>

            <section id="changes"><h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy as JolaxPay’s services, providers or legal obligations change. We will publish the revised version here and update the effective date. Where a change is material, we may also notify you in the app, by email or through another appropriate channel.</p></section>

            <section id="contact"><h2>13. Contact us</h2><p>For privacy questions, account-data requests or concerns about how your information is handled, contact JolaxPay using the details below.</p><div class="contact"><h3>JolaxPay Privacy & Support</h3><p>Email: <a href="mailto:support@jolaxpay.com">support@jolaxpay.com</a><br>You may also open a support ticket from within the JolaxPay mobile app.</p><p>If your concern is not resolved, you may lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://ndpc.gov.ng/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nigeria Data Protection Commission</a>.</p></div></section>
